# Absent agent/metadata probe paths -> a real 404, NOT the app.
#
# The catch-all at the bottom makes real routes like /defi-forge work on a single-page
# site. Its side effect: ANY missing path returned 200 plus the full homepage, so an
# automated client asking "do you have an llms.txt?" was told yes and handed HTML.
#
# The destination is not-found.html, NOT 404.html, and the name is the whole point.
# On 2026-08-18 a root 404.html was added here and took down every deep route: Cloudflare
# Pages adopts a root 404.html as its own not-found handler, which pre-empts the SPA
# rewrite. Renaming the file keeps the 404 body without triggering that behaviour.
#
# Listed explicitly rather than by a wildcard such as /*.json: splat semantics for
# mid-path patterns are unverified here and an over-broad rule would break routing.
/llms.txt                 /not-found.html   404
/llms-full.txt            /not-found.html   404
/agents.json              /not-found.html   404
/agent.json               /not-found.html   404
/ucp.json                 /not-found.html   404
/acp.json                 /not-found.html   404
/openapi.json             /not-found.html   404
/mcp.json                 /not-found.html   404
/.well-known/*            /not-found.html   404

# Single-page app fallback - every real route is served by index.html.
/*    /index.html   200
